{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790265012,"nonce":"iZtxHkM4q/ujbIXooJCUsonfirQ=","message":"The API surface is complete. Landed in 2edcdc3, 3b06431, 7626bee, 189d1c5, 26152c1 and 7ddac2d.\n\n- Bindgen: `#[extension]` fields, enum values and union alternatives; explicit constants in a `mod`; a static function can take a record first.\n- Pipelines and passes: render and compute pipelines from WebGPU's descriptors, sync and async; render and compute pass descriptors with load/store, resolve targets, read-only depth-stencil, timestamps and occlusion; full draw ranges, multi-draw and multi-draw-count, immediates.\n- Queries, bundles, copies: occlusion, timestamp and pipeline statistics query sets, encoder and pass timestamps, resolve; render bundles; texture copies with origin, mip level, aspect and buffer layout; clearTexture; writeTextureWith.\n- Errors and loss: error scopes as futures, device.lost with Destroyed after destroy(), structured compilation messages.\n- Surfaces: capabilities (formats, present and alpha modes, usages) and configureSurfaceWith (usage, view formats, present and alpha mode, color space, frame latency).\n- wgpu's own: NativeFeature generated from wgpu's flags, NativeLimit, texture format features and usages, extension formats (R64uint, NV12, P010, Float64 vertices), ClampToBorder and border colours, atomic storage textures, polygon mode and conservative rasterisation, binding arrays, external textures, mesh pipelines and mesh draws, BLAS/TLAS creation, builds, binding and compaction.\n- Experimental features: requesting an EXPERIMENTAL_* native feature turns on wgpu's experimental token for that device only.\n- Introspection and options: instance backends and flags, adapter options with a compatible surface, memory hints, adapter PCI ids, device type and subgroup sizes, buffer and texture getters, map-for-write and copyIn.\n\nChecked on Apple M1 Pro/Metal (gpu fixture, also under ASH_GC_STRESS=1 WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1; window_gpu presents); clippy with warnings denied for macOS, Linux x86_64, Windows MSVC and wasm32-unknown-unknown; bindgen and GPU unit tests on macOS and Linux.\n\nNot exposed, listed in the plugin README: members wgpu 30 lacks (component swizzle, binding view dimension, map state, label read-back), API tracing, browser image sources, the sequence spelling of GPUExtent3D.\n\nFollow-ups:\n- git-bug: ead67ccb79dd8d9360ca3ef81113b8038d6f61bfa7512bd7d0a9ef30637a64c5 (bindgen generation of interface operations, callbacks, unions, conversions)\n- git-bug: 78856284ea3a597dcf3d733b8a11258874642901099223edb05f14ed93e30f06 (browser runtime, mobile handles, runtime checks off Apple)\n- git-bug: 380813c9fad405e6c61091ab3a7f4329eb7acfefa0a6bd30a41d65bdf9bca9a9 (wgpu's unsafe-only entry points)","files":null}]}